+\subsubsection{Repeated-task study, primary comparison, and workflow ablations}
+
+The repeated-task study compares Guided, Standard, Record, and Brief-errors on E1, NB1, HA1, and IA1, with three independent runs per combination (48 runs). Its elapsed-time unit is a four-task batch at a concurrency of two, with three batches per configuration. The full-benchmark study retains one run for each of the 50 tasks and four configurations (200 runs). The primary comparison is Guided against the actual Standard branch using the same model backbone. Standard hides explicit DAG tools, removes scientific acceptance interception, and supplies neutral computational feedback. Guided retains the research graph, scientific checks, and detailed diagnostics. Record preserves available tools and records while removing mandatory acceptance; Brief-errors retains guidance while shortening diagnostics. Common task statements and method restrictions apply across configurations; run versions, budgets, stopping reasons, and artifact provenance are retained in the archive.
